## Input

data = [('Goa', ' ' ,'AP'), (' ' ,'AP','None'), ('None', '  ' ,'bglr')]
columns = ["city1", "city2", "city3"]

df = spark.createDataFrame(data, columns)
display(df)

Input data:
+-----+-----+-----+
|city1|city2|city3|
+-----+-----+-----+
|Goa  |     |AP   |
|     |AP   |None |
|None |     |bglr |
+-----+-----+-----+


Solution:

from pyspark.sql.functions import coalesce, when, col

df1 = df.withColumn(
    "firstnotnull",
    coalesce(
        when((col("city1").rlike("^\\s*$")) | (col("city1") == "None"), None).otherwise(col("city1")),
        when((col("city2").rlike("^\\s*$")) | (col("city2") == "None"), None).otherwise(col("city2")),
        when((col("city3").rlike("^\\s*$")) | (col("city3") == "None"), None).otherwise(col("city3"))
    ))
df1.show(truncate=False)


OUTPUT:
+-----+-----+-----+-------------+
|city1|city2|city3|firstnotnull |
+-----+-----+-----+-------------+
|Goa  |     |AP   |Goa          |
|     |AP   |None |AP           |
|None |     |bglr |bglr         |
+-----+-----+-----+-------------+


